{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias beyond ~1 week: the model systematically underpredicts medium-term rebounds/rallies. Apply an upward level adjustment that grows with horizon (small in days 1–5, larger from ~day 10 onward).",
    "Trend/turning-point lag: after a local bottom, the model turns up too slowly and misses the speed of recovery. If the last 5–10 days show a clear downswing into a trough, steepen the subsequent 1–3 week forecast slope upward.",
    "Underestimation of upside volatility: the model captures early path but misses later upside extensions (notably days ~20–30). Add a positive convexity term (increasing uplift) when recent realized volatility is elevated and momentum flips positive.",
    "Mean-reversion too strong / ceiling too low: forecasts revert toward low/mid-60s even when outcomes trend to upper-60s. Raise the implied long-run mean when the last observed price is below the 20–30d average but outcomes historically rebound.",
    "Horizon-specific correction: days 1–5 errors are small; the main miss is accumulation over days 10–30. Concentrate corrections on the back half of the forecast window rather than uniformly shifting the whole path."
  ]
}
